  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study visit on horticulture in the Rabat-Sal&#xe9;-K&#xe9;nitra and Larache region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Goal of this study visit is for the Moroccan participants to get acquainted with the Dutch horticultural sector and the triple helix approach. This will be done by knowledge exchange and making the MAR government familiar with the  Dutch combi-track approach in Morocco. As a result, the collaboration between Dutch and Moroccan stakeholders during the implementation of the combi-track activities will be strengthened.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this study visit, a Moroccan delegation of decision makers in the agricultural sector will be informed about the organisation of the horticultural sector in the Netherlands and its current development and working methods.The mission includes visits to (government) institutions and companies active in different value chains of the horticultural sectors, research institutions, clusters and branche organisations.The aim is to introduce climate-smart, water-smart and sustainable growing techniques from the Netherlands and contribute to efficient water use and sustainable energy to make food production more sustainable.Moreover, the visit will enable the participants to establish direct contacts with the representatives in the Dutch horticultural sector and enable both parties to discuss and develop joint proposals for creation of Dutch-Moroccan horticultural activities in the regions of Rabat-Sale-Kenitra-Larache region.</narrative>
  </description>
